convict|declare-guilty|VERB|declare guilty in court|Officially decide in court that a person is guilty of a crime.|tuyên có tội; kết tội|The jury convicted the driver of fraud.|Bồi thẩm đoàn kết tội người lái xe về hành vi gian lận.|Transitive; convict somebody of a crime, often also in the passive form be convicted of.|convict
directly|without-intermediary|ADVERB|without an intermediate step|Without passing through an intermediary or taking a detour on the way to a person or place.|trực tiếp; thẳng tới|The shuttle takes passengers directly to the ferry terminal.|Xe đưa đón chở hành khách thẳng tới bến phà.|Directly to identifies the destination; this draft covers direct contact or route, not the time sense.|directly
closed|not-open|ADJECTIVE|not open for access|Unavailable for people to enter or use at a particular time.|đóng cửa; không cho vào hoặc sử dụng|The swimming pool is closed during the winter.|Bể bơi đóng cửa trong mùa đông.|Often used after be; closed for repairs explains a reason and closed on a day states a schedule.|closed
dissatisfied|not-satisfied|ADJECTIVE|not satisfied|Unhappy because something falls short of what was wanted or expected.|không hài lòng; không thỏa mãn|Several customers were dissatisfied with the slow delivery.|Một số khách hàng không hài lòng vì giao hàng chậm.|Use dissatisfied with something to name the cause of the feeling.|dissatisfied
stiff|restricted-movement|ADJECTIVE|difficult to move freely|Feeling tight or uncomfortable and unable to move as freely as usual.|cứng; khó cử động ở cơ thể|My neck felt stiff after I slept on the sofa.|Cổ tôi bị cứng sau khi ngủ trên ghế sofa.|Used with body parts or muscles; feel stiff describes a physical condition rather than rigid material.|stiff
stiff|rigid-material|ADJECTIVE|difficult to bend|Firm enough to resist bending or folding easily.|cứng; khó uốn|We used stiff paper to make the model stand upright.|Chúng tôi dùng giấy cứng để mô hình đứng thẳng.|Used before a material noun or after be; this sense concerns rigidity rather than sore muscles.|stiff
translate|change-language|VERB|express in another language|Express the meaning of spoken or written words using a different language.|dịch sang ngôn ngữ khác|Mai translated the museum notice into English.|Mai dịch thông báo của bảo tàng sang tiếng Anh.|Transitive; translate something from one language into another names the source and target languages.|translate
ambassador|diplomatic-representative|NOUN|diplomatic representative|An official who represents their country in another country.|đại sứ|The ambassador attended a meeting at the host country's parliament.|Đại sứ dự một cuộc họp tại quốc hội nước sở tại.|Countable; ambassador to a country identifies where the official represents their government.|ambassador
contractor|contracted-provider|NOUN|provider under a contract|A person or business hired under an agreement to supply work, goods or services.|nhà thầu; bên cung cấp theo hợp đồng|The contractor replaced the damaged windows in our office.|Nhà thầu thay những cửa sổ bị hỏng trong văn phòng chúng tôi.|Countable; building work is a common context, but the source also supports other contracted supplies or services.|contractor
illustrate|explain-visually|VERB|make clear with an example or image|Make an idea or situation easier to understand by showing examples or visual information.|minh họa; làm rõ bằng ví dụ hoặc hình ảnh|This diagram illustrates how rainwater reaches the tank.|Sơ đồ này minh họa cách nước mưa chảy vào bể.|Transitive; a diagram, photograph or example can illustrate an idea or show how something works.|illustrate
illustrate|provide-pictures|VERB|provide pictures for a publication|Create the pictures that accompany the text of a publication.|vẽ minh họa cho sách hoặc ấn phẩm|A local artist illustrated the children's poetry collection.|Một họa sĩ địa phương vẽ minh họa cho tập thơ thiếu nhi.|Transitive; illustrate a book or collection focuses on making its accompanying pictures.|illustrate
engagement|participation|NOUN|active participation|Active involvement in an activity, discussion or community.|sự tham gia; sự gắn kết|The reading project encouraged parents' engagement in school activities.|Dự án đọc sách khuyến khích phụ huynh tham gia các hoạt động ở trường.|Usually uncountable in this sense; engagement in an activity or with a community names the involvement.|engagement
engagement|betrothal|NOUN|agreement to marry|An agreement by two people to marry, or the period following that agreement.|sự đính hôn; thời gian đính hôn|Their engagement lasted a year before the wedding.|Họ đính hôn một năm trước khi tổ chức đám cưới.|Often their engagement or an engagement to somebody; this concerns a marriage agreement.|engagement
engagement|appointment|NOUN|arranged commitment|An arrangement to attend an event or carry out an activity at a particular time.|cuộc hẹn; lịch hẹn đã nhận lời|The historian cancelled a speaking engagement because she was ill.|Nhà sử học hủy lịch hẹn phát biểu vì bà bị ốm.|Countable; a speaking engagement is an arranged commitment to give a talk.|engagement
end|final-point|NOUN|final part or point|The last part or point of an event, period or thing.|phần cuối; điểm kết thúc|At the end of the workshop, we displayed our clay bowls.|Cuối buổi thực hành, chúng tôi trưng bày những chiếc bát đất sét của mình.|Countable; the end of something identifies its final part or point.|end
end|finish|VERB|finish or bring to a finish|Reach a finish or cause something to finish.|kết thúc; chấm dứt|The organizer ended the discussion when the lights went out.|Người tổ chức kết thúc cuộc thảo luận khi đèn tắt.|Transitive or intransitive; end a discussion and a discussion ends describe causing or reaching a finish.|end
eye|sight-organ|NOUN|organ of sight|One of the organs through which a person or animal sees.|mắt|The puppy opened its eyes and looked at the light.|Chú chó con mở mắt và nhìn về phía ánh sáng.|Countable; the plural eyes refers to both organs, while an eye refers to one.|eye
villain|evil-person|NOUN|evil person or character|A person, especially a fictional character, who deliberately harms others or commits serious wrongdoing.|kẻ ác; nhân vật phản diện|The villain in the play secretly stole the villagers' savings.|Kẻ ác trong vở kịch bí mật lấy cắp tiền tiết kiệm của dân làng.|Countable; in a story this denotes an evil character, rather than every person opposing the main character.|villain
processing|information-handling|NOUN|work on information|Organized work that transforms or arranges information to produce a useful result.|việc xử lý thông tin|The new server reduced the time needed for image processing.|Máy chủ mới rút ngắn thời gian cần để xử lý hình ảnh.|Uncountable; image processing and data processing name kinds of work on information.|processing
processing|material-treatment|NOUN|treatment of materials|Operations that prepare or change materials so they can be used, preserved or dealt with.|việc xử lý vật liệu; sự chế biến|The factory installed equipment for the processing of vegetables.|Nhà máy lắp thiết bị để chế biến rau củ.|Uncountable; food processing is one application, while the source also supports treatment of other materials.|processing
oversee|supervise|VERB|supervise work|Watch and direct a task or activity to make sure it is carried out properly.|giám sát; trông nom công việc|An experienced librarian oversaw the move to the new building.|Một thủ thư giàu kinh nghiệm giám sát việc chuyển sang tòa nhà mới.|Transitive; past oversaw and past participle overseen; oversee a project or operation.|oversee
percentage|share-out-of-hundred|NOUN|share expressed out of a hundred|A share of a whole stated as a number out of one hundred.|tỷ lệ phần trăm|The report shows the percentage of homes with solar panels.|Báo cáo cho biết tỷ lệ phần trăm nhà có tấm pin mặt trời.|Countable; percentage of a group names the proportion, without itself specifying the actual number.|percentage
scramble|hurry-with-effort|VERB|move hurriedly with effort|Move somewhere in a hurried and effortful way, often without an orderly plan.|chạy hoặc di chuyển vội vã; chen lấn|We scrambled up the bank as the river began to rise.|Chúng tôi vội leo lên bờ khi nước sông bắt đầu dâng.|Intransitive here; a direction phrase such as up or toward identifies where the hurried movement goes.|scramble
two|cardinal-number|NUMBER|cardinal number two|The number formed by adding one and one.|hai|Please put two cushions on the wooden bench.|Vui lòng đặt hai chiếc đệm lên ghế dài bằng gỗ.|A cardinal number before a plural countable noun; source NUMBER remains a draft proposal, not a canonical taxonomy decision.|two
patriot|devoted-to-country|NOUN|person devoted to their country|A person with strong affection for and commitment to their country.|người yêu nước; nhà ái quốc|As a patriot, he wanted to improve public education in his country.|Là người yêu nước, ông muốn cải thiện giáo dục công ở đất nước mình.|Countable; the term describes devotion to a country and does not require a military role.|patriot
inn|traveller-lodging|NOUN|small lodging place for travellers|A small place where travellers can rent rooms and usually obtain meals.|nhà trọ; quán trọ có chỗ nghỉ|We booked a room at a quiet inn beside the harbour.|Chúng tôi đặt phòng ở một quán trọ yên tĩnh cạnh bến cảng.|Countable; stay at an inn describes lodging, rather than eating at any restaurant.|inn
